        "id": 117242,
        "name": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
        "username": "BlueHairedMeerkat",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluehairedmeerkat/{size}/1967_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-08T19:45:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Regardless, you have yet to give a good alternative to \"indestructible.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Just leaving that there. There is no better term. Also, while six-sided cards are a great straw man, the word 'destroy' is a better example. One does not rip a card to pieces when it's destroyed; you look up what the word means in the context of the game. That's just how games work.</p>",
