        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Matchstickman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/48/1880_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Matchstickman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Greywind wrote:</b><br><blockquote><em>Highlander TCG</em> tournaments involved a format known as <em>The Iron Man</em>. If, during the course of the tournament, your Immortal lost his head, you were obligated to destroy your persona card.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nHighlander itself is also used as a type of tournament.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes. One of each card except basic lands.</p>\n<p>I believe Magic has also used Iron Man format unofficially.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
