      {
        "id": 117251,
        "name": "jagarciao",
        "username": "jagarciao",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/{size}/2010_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-09T12:27:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Unsafe_Bet\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/u/53a042/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Unsafe_Bet:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;We already have to mentally rewrite the rules on the cards in the case of old copies of Solar Flare etc. (since the replacement cards are the wrong size and can't actually replace them).&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I believe the size incompatibility of the replacement cards is only an issue for earlier printings of the game, which had cards that were slightly larger than the standard card size. At least in my case, the replacement cards fit perfectly with my more recently acquired decks for Ra and Fanatic.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>As far as the \"indestructible\" thing, I see the point you are making, but I don't believe there's a better keyword for it. Any word you use will require you to look up its in-game definition at some point (like you have to for most other game terms even when they are common words: \"what does destroy mean? Does it go out of the game completely or just in the discard pile? OK, then what does discard mean?\"), and will probably cause more questions about its interaction with the \"destroy\" action than \"indestructible\" does about its interaction with non-\"destroy\" game-removing actions.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
