      {
        "id": 117258,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-01T19:39:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Any target can be reduced to 0hp or fewer - note on several villain cards it says \"When X is reduced to 0hp or fewer, flip this card\" or whatever (I think Apostate's flip condition says that, which is how you can get away with insta-killing him via Suckerpunch or other such cards since then you're not reducing his hp, you're just destroying him). It's just that normally you don't continue counting once you get to 0hp because any overkill damage in the hit isn't really needed.</p>\n<p>With Fixed Point, you track the hp into the negatives and, as Pydro says, if a target goes into the negatives but then heals back up again to at least 1hp by the time Fixed Point goes away, that target isn't destroyed. Any targets that <span class=\"bbcode-i\">are</span> at 0hp or fewer when Fixed Point goes away suddenly go \"Oh crap, I have no hitpoints left, urgghhhh\" :D.</p>",
        "post_number": 37,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:49:54.612Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 0.2,
